From 0f906a452700b21d3e52a9d094e52c7cb9a19a1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: skornuta <126527569+skornuta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:04:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/27] Bindless eviction: the queue parks, not makes, slots of
 textures let go unread

Every evicted copy made again now notes its call path (`REMADE`, the
memory minute lists the most common). A 3-minute run named one: of
~14,500 copies made again, all of the top paths went through
`State::heap_textures` -> `HostHeap::mirror` -> `make`: the texture queue
serving title slots that show the texture but had no host slot when it
was let go (so were not parked), due again when the title wrote them or
the texture's memory changed - no shader asking.

A texture let go while no shader read any of its slots is marked (the
frame it went; cleared when it is made again). When the queue comes to a
slot of such a texture it parks that slot too (with its view's key) and
takes it out of the due slots, unless the feedback saw a shader read that
very slot since; a draw through a table, a shader read, or another view
written into the slot make it as before.

The memory CSV gets `fb_queue_parked`.

(cherry picked from commit 79dc3be705370e4d6769042e66f65f7447c3e3bd)
